/--
Once a compact schedule retains no dyadic levels past `cutoff`, its source
shell coupling splits into a finite effective-count head and the explicit
fifth-order coarse transport tail.  This is a deterministic bridge: the
probability cost of the zero-depth tail is already zero, while the finite head
